WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
- What people don't know,
what followers don't know,

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.603
is as bloggers you borrow pieces.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.750
So they would see Lamborghini
lending me a car for a week

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.550
and be like, "oh my god, he's like 23,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.820
and he's driving a Lamborghini,
this kid's balling."

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:11.833
That's not the case.

00:00:12.058 --> 00:00:15.808
(glamorous electronic music)

00:00:16.277 --> 00:00:18.630
My name is Mahmoud Sidani,
my friends call me Moudz,

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.660
I am the top men's
fashion lifestyle blogger

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.573
for the Middle East.

00:00:22.573 --> 00:00:25.070
If ever I meet someone that
doesn't know what a blogger is,

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.380
I describe it as someone who has following

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.593
that allows them to influence people.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.100
Brands work with me in order
to help shape their opinions

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.720
and shed a light on their
products and their services.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.690
I'm from Beirut, Lebanon, but
I grew up in Saudi Arabia.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.050
My mom works with NGOs
around the Middle East

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:45.240
and my dad was heading
Research and Development

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.780
for an oil company in
Saudi Arabia for 30 years.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.950
I moved to Dubai six years ago to be

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.980
a buyer for Level Shoes, which is

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.270
the biggest shoe store in the world.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.560
It introduced me to a
lot of influential people

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.480
who have really shaped
the fashion industry.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.900
I was with them for three years,

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.500
until I decided to open a store.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.130
After I resigned, I realized
that I wasn't ready.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.000
So I was stuck, I was
like, what am I gonna do?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.945
At that point I was
approached by a brand who

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:13.320
doesn't really fit with
the Mr. Moudz brand.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.870
In order to get them off my back,

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.570
I threw a ridiculous number at them.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.060
They were like, "okay, we'll
do it," and I was shocked.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.370
It's then that I realized
that there was something here

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:24.450
that hasn't been tapped into
in terms of a men's blogger.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.090
To this day, there aren't many of us,

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:28.430
in comparison to how many
there are in the female market.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:30.410
I do Barry's Bootcamp five times a week.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.013
I then come back home,
shower, have breakfast.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.940
And then, day starts, from
fittings to photo shoots,

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.363
to meetings with brands,

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.070
and then everyday I
try and make it a point

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:41.580
to see my nieces and nephew.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.150
My family is my number one supporter.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.680
My mom loved it from the get-go.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.580
She introduces herself as
Mama Moudz, it's really cute.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.510
And I'm like, mom, that's
not like saying you're, like,

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.500
Beyonce's mother.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.110
I'm fortunate to have relationships

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.420
with all major luxury brands.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.750
I'm very guilty when it comes
to shoes, I have way too many.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.613
Right now, it's the Don
C's that I'm wearing.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.870
They're so simple but
they really stand out.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:05.443
We are about to go to a Nike event,

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.993
followed by a Dior event,
and then now we're gonna try

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:08.920
and make it to the Christian
Loubotin event as well.

00:02:10.106 --> 00:02:11.833
We have a busy day, so let's go.

00:02:11.949 --> 00:02:14.680
(crunchy Middle Eastern
influenced electronic music)

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.550
I'm lucky enough to be at these events.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.550
I see things ahead of their release day,

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.370
or I get to do experience,
like I think today

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.263
we're customizing Nike shoes,
which should be really cool.

00:02:31.648 --> 00:02:32.620
(camera clicks)

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:36.003
Don C just signed my Don C by Nike shoes.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.144
This is a really big deal,
that's like getting Kanye

00:02:38.144 --> 00:02:40.144
to sign Yeezy's for you.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.620
My proudest moment was last year.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.250
I was able to take my
whole family on vacation

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.083
to the Maldives.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.440
And this was on a blogger's expense,

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.310
where the hotel was given to us for free,

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.540
flights were given to us for free,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.000
just because I would be tagging them.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.300
My dad got so upset with me on that trip

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.260
because I wasn't enjoying the moment,

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.740
I was too busy trying to get the shot,

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.627
and he was like, "enjoy it.

00:03:00.627 --> 00:03:02.427
"Take this in here in the Maldives."

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.230
And, that was an eye-opener.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.120
So now, if I'm traveling,
and it is a sponsored hotel,

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.930
I'll get the shots done in
the first half of the day

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.280
and then I'll get to
enjoy the rest of my trip.

00:03:22.725 --> 00:03:25.142
And then, I bid you farewell.

00:03:25.495 --> 00:03:27.397
(cameraman laughs)
And cry a little.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.420
- You're somewhat
categorized and put in a box.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.640
Not to say that they're limiting you,

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.400
but they just have an image of what

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.913
a male persona should be.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.620
When I first started, a lot of
people were asking questions,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.287
like, "this is not like
a lot of other guys,"

00:03:45.287 --> 00:03:46.550
"this is not what we're used to seeing."

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:49.320
You get to really open up people's eyes

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.880
and change their opinions
to what should be accepted

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:52.990
in terms of fashion.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.690
I've always wanted to
be my own individual,

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.620
I wanted to take things that a lot of guys

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.850
wouldn't really wear and
say, look, it could work.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.630
I'm not waiting for someone else

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.820
to tell me that it looks good
to think that it looks good.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.083
I was bullied as a kid.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.760
I wasn't like the other
boys, I wasn't into sports.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.470
I would rather talk about clothes.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.110
It's nothing to do with the
Middle East, it's worldwide.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.523
People are so eager to categorize you.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.103
And when you don't fit into that box,

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.150
that's just extra paperwork for
them, so it pisses them off.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.930
That's why right now I'm so all about

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:22.570
live the life you wanna
live, and be happy,

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.240
because at the end of
the day that relationship

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.390
you have with yourself are the
most important relationship

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:27.390
you'll ever work on.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.940
I was broken until three years ago.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.450
It was only recently that
I learned to heal myself.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.140
I was looking for the
fame because I thought

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.660
this would fill that void in me.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.760
When the fame came, I somewhat
got uncomfortable with it

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:40.850
at one point because I feel like

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.360
it's a real invasion of privacy.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.740
But what I learned was,
all along, I had the power

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:45.960
to fill that void myself.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.570
It was part of my journey
to become a blogger.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.840
I don't claim to know it
all, but I've learned a lot,

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.700
and a lot of what I've
learned can help others.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:55.380
Today I did everything
that was on my to-do list,

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:58.190
tomorrow gotta come back to
Sole DXB in the afternoon

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.993
and shoot some looks.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.020
It's just ongoing, it never stops.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.647
People think that blogging is just like,

00:05:03.647 --> 00:05:04.963
you're just having fun.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.250
If you do it properly it's
actually a lot of work.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.510
Some days you do get tired,
some days you're like,

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.812
do I wanna keep doing this, do
I wanna keep putting my life

00:05:11.812 --> 00:05:14.613
in the public light and
opening myself up for judgment?

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.283
But you just need to think
about why you started.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.890
I started doing this because
I wanted to make a change.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.040
I wanted people to see
me doing what I'm doing,

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.157
see me doing my own thing and say,

00:05:23.157 --> 00:05:25.757
"you know what, if he did it, then I can."

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.690
- I've definitely contributed something

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.293
to changing opinions for sure.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:35.960
I think everyone has.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.810
You have no idea how many
times I've been stopped

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.970
at the airport for
random security checking

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.450
because my name is Mahmoud.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.800
Or I'll have a conversation with someone,

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.707
all begin to say, like,
"oh my god, you're Arab?

00:05:46.707 --> 00:05:48.940
"Your English is perfect." (sighs)

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.340
It just shocks me that some people are not

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:56.330
as educated with other parts in the world.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.400
It's a two-sided thing,
it's not a one-sided thing.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.380
But I do hope that I'm
changing that, people's views,

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.610
because I wanna leave this Earth

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.033
having said that I was here.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.365
I wanna leave it better
than how I found it.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:10.115
(energetic electronic music)

